menu "STARK"

    choice STARK_BOARD
        prompt "Board variant"
        default STARK_BOARD_DEVKITC1
        help
            Selects the pin map and stark_board_init() implementation from
            components/stark_board. Pin values are normative in
            HARDWARE.md §2 and must not be duplicated elsewhere in the
            firmware (AGENTS.md).

        config STARK_BOARD_DEVKITC1
            bool "ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1 (development target, also used by Wokwi)"
    endchoice

    # STARK_DISPLAY_BAND_H and STARK_DISPLAY_SPI_HZ are, by name and by
    # ARCHITECTURE.md §9, stark_display's Kconfig symbols. stark_display
    # does not exist yet, but stark_board_init() genuinely needs a byte
    # count for spi_bus_initialize()'s max_transfer_sz *now* (TASKS.md
    # STARK-0006: "max transfer = 320 * BAND_H * 2"). Declared here
    # temporarily so the real mechanism (Kconfig, not a hardcoded C
    # constant) is used without inventing any display driver code.
    # Move both symbols to stark_display's own Kconfig when it exists.

    config STARK_DISPLAY_BAND_H
        int "Display render band height (lines)"
        default 40
        help
            Height of one DMA render band, in scanlines. Sizes the SPI2
            bus max transfer: 320 * STARK_DISPLAY_BAND_H * 2 bytes
            (default 25600). See ARCHITECTURE.md §9, HARDWARE.md §2.3.

    config STARK_DISPLAY_SPI_HZ
        int "Display SPI clock (Hz)"
        default 20000000
        help
            SPI2 bus clock for the panel. HARDWARE.md §2.3: 40 MHz on the
            production PCB, 20 MHz on breadboard — long jumper wires will
            not survive 40 MHz. The devkitc1 board variant is a
            breadboard target, hence 20 MHz here; this intentionally
            differs from ARCHITECTURE.md §9's PCB-oriented 40 MHz table
            default, which applies once STARK_BOARD_PCB_R1 exists.

endmenu
